---
title: "Primary-Backup Key-Value Service | Go"
layout: post
---

I implemented a fault-tolerant key-value store by replicating data over a primary and backup server, using a view service to coordinate server roles, monitor liveness via periodic heartbeat pings, and manage view transitions during failures and restarts. The primary handles all client requests and forwards updates to the backup, ensuring the backup is ready to take over if necessary. When a new backup is selected, the primary transfers the complete key-value state to it. Servers detect role changes by periodically pinging the view service, and provide at-most-once semantics by tracking client IDs and sequence numbers for each request.